# PART 1 — PRODUCT IDENTITY AND DESIGN SYSTEM

## 1.1 Raqimo identity

Raqimo is an AI-powered Business Operating System for freelancers, independent professionals, and small businesses.

Its purpose is to help business owners manage their customers, money, projects, daily operations, and business decisions from one connected workspace.

The experience should feel:

- Premium.
- Minimal.
- Intelligent.
- Professional.
- Modern.
- Smooth.
- Fast.
- Intuitive for non-technical users.
- Powerful enough for experienced project managers.

The product should not look like a generic admin dashboard, an Odoo clone, or a Jira clone.

It should have its own recognizable design language.

## 1.2 Existing design identity — mandatory

Preserve the existing Raqimo branding.

Main colors:

- Primary blue: #2680EB
- Secondary cyan: #1FA6C9
- Emerald green: #10B981
- Dark background: #050505
- Dark elevated surfaces: #0F0F0F
- Main text: #F0F0F0
- Light background: #F4F6F8
- Light text: #0B1220

Primary CTA buttons must use the Raqimo blue-to-cyan-to-emerald gradient.

Use the same gradient family already used by the existing sign-in experience.

Do not introduce an unrelated purple, orange, or generic SaaS color palette.

## 1.3 Visual language

The default experience must be dark.

Use:

- Black backgrounds.
- Subtle glassmorphism.
- Translucent surfaces.
- Soft gradient highlights.
- Thin borders.
- Carefully controlled shadows.
- Modern rounded corners.
- Elegant hover states.
- Smooth transitions.
- Clear visual hierarchy.
- Compact but comfortable spacing.

Glassy design must be subtle and functional, not excessive.

Use glass effects for:

- Floating toolbars.
- Context menus.
- Dropdowns.
- Command palettes.
- Modals.
- Selected cards.
- Quick-action panels.
- Floating creation controls.

Do not make every surface transparent. Content must remain readable.

Cards should have clear separation from their background.

## 1.4 Responsive design

Every page must work properly on:

- Large desktop monitors.
- Standard laptops.
- Tablets.
- Mobile devices.

Desktop:
Use the full sidebar, page toolbar, multi-column layouts, and expanded data tables.

Tablet:
Adapt grids, collapse secondary navigation, and preserve usable interactions.

Mobile:
Use compact navigation, horizontally scrollable board columns where appropriate, full-screen creation forms when necessary, bottom sheets, and touch-friendly actions.

Never allow tables, dialogs, kanban boards, or toolbars to overflow the viewport unintentionally.

## 1.5 Theme support

Preserve the existing dark/light theme implementation.

Every new component must support both themes.

Dark theme:
- Black and charcoal surfaces.
- White primary text.
- Muted gray secondary text.
- Subtle white borders.

Light theme:
- Soft neutral backgrounds.
- White elevated cards.
- Dark readable typography.
- Proper border contrast.
- No invisible axis labels, text, icons, or dropdown items.

Never hardcode dark-mode-only colors into components that should respond to the theme.

Use semantic theme tokens wherever possible.

## 1.6 Language and RTL

Preserve the existing English/Arabic language switch.

Every new feature must support:

- English LTR.
- Arabic RTL.
- Correct Arabic typography.
- Proper text alignment.
- Logical spacing.
- Reversed directional navigation where appropriate.
- Correct placement of dropdowns, drawers, and side panels.

Do not simply translate labels while leaving the layout in LTR.

Use logical CSS properties rather than physical left/right assumptions wherever possible.

Arabic should feel like a first-class product experience.

